# Layer 2 (profile) for `va local --profile windows-native` — the current
# AMD/Windows setup: whisper.cpp (Vulkan) + piper (DirectML) + ollama run as
# NATIVE processes via scripts/Start-VoiceAssistant.ps1; nothing is dockered.
# Sits between deploy/.env.example (layer 1) and the per-host secrets file
# %USERPROFILE%\.config\va\deploy.env (layer 3); later layers win.
# See docs/deploy-architecture.md, "Env-Layering".
#
# Native service knobs (paths, model, ports) are read by
# scripts/lib/VaLocalConfig.ps1 — shared by Start-VoiceAssistant.ps1,
# check-services.ps1, Setup-VoiceAssistant.ps1 and deploy/va.ps1. Defaults live
# there; host-specific values (VA_WHISPER_DIR, VA_WHISPER_MODEL,
# VA_PIPER_PYTHON, PIPER_VOICES_DIR, VA_VAULT_PATH, ...) are written to
# %USERPROFILE%\.config\va\deploy.env by `scripts/Setup-VoiceAssistant.ps1`.
# deploy/.env.example is NOT layered in for the native path (it carries
# compose hostnames such as RAG_URL=http://rag:5001). The launcher exports
# WHISPER_URL/TTS_URL/OLLAMA_URL/RAG_URL/OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH to the node server,
# overriding apps/server/.env (process env beats dotenv) so launcher ports and
# server URLs can never drift apart.

# No CUDA on this box — piper runs DirectML natively.
PIPER_USE_CUDA=0

# Compose-only knobs that mean nothing natively (documented, not needed):
# REGISTRY / IMAGE_TAG / *_VISIBLE_DEVICES are ignored by the native path.
